a21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "42f277b3-3b0c-5696-a11e-305bac244d37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326294/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "12d78cb7-13bd-55b5-9308-8fdee0296020" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326294/field-4/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-326294/field-4/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326294" :question/id #uuid "7fd11da8-69ae-58b7-a146-e95c709d162a" :question/math-academy-id "q-326294" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ngiven that the general solution to our differential equation is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{-t}.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=5 \\\\ {c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n5{c}_{1}=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n2\\cdot 1+{c}_{2}=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-326294/field-1" "q-326294/field-2" "q-326294/field-3" "q-326294/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83399378-8815-5602-a60a-6901114416f7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-326294"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-326002/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "cb486f53-5ec0-52e0-a53a-b4ec38c992ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326002/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "529329e1-dc83-565e-b1db-6fc9f714b16a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186131125 :answer-field/correct "q-326002/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-326002/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-326002/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326002/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "330d9960-10c9-5996-a6b3-f6419cadfb3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186131124 :answer-field/correct "q-326002/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer