c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+3{c}_{2} \\\\ 2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+3{c}_{2}=5 \\\\ 2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $-2$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-7{c}_{2}=-7\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+3\\cdot 1=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-326295/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "69a8b8b2-2aea-55fb-a36e-f86cc392580d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326295/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a462bd57-ae87-5df1-9e7a-04291078a34b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326295/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-326295/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326295/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "55ad3313-b96f-57bb-baf6-108c197b7c40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326295/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a