d7fdbdfc5e8acd2ebc49c992" "q-79733/selection/9a41dbf55903320ded97f4b55e8e2740e6a5f57ebb04b1c3afbbec8811f11be2" "q-79733/selection/3c6d4bdc545512243e610249077d36385cc5451706da1587c8362c9b5149edf0" "q-79733/selection/bff30d89f04bdf1d7e861c292df8dcdd80720d88d71dac11c0ff800217717203"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79733" :question/id #uuid "cbc7fbb6-5ecf-5e40-98fc-81b2c93a104a" :question/math-academy-id "q-79733" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2$ corresponding to the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ respectively, where\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=4 \\\\ {c}_{1}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n4\\cdot 3+{c}_{2}=4\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=-8.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution for the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+(-8)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79733/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35a8694d-4fa1-54a6-a492-3025cb627fa1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79733"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186134130 :question/answer-fields 17592186131222] {:db/id "q-39240/selection/ma-v1/2671d331d97c53f2375612cbe37f808e089924829a937b7c66c1f6d012bbb6f3/03405750d53422e5f900264a3b5790d3243a6d48620aa6b73d0b474408d49b87" :answer/id #uuid "e989a718-9f0d-504d-906d-ff2a25950e72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39240/selection/ma-v1/2671d331d97c53f2375612cbe37f808e089924829a937b7c66c1f6d012bbb6f3/8f51c79b2e0be63ce4fd1113e3a43575ad632facb9460c2e70f895df8b581242" :answer/id #uuid "a8d777ed-4249-5a10-b0a7-8206bf3417f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39240/selection/ma-v1/2671d331d97c53f2375612cbe37f808e089924829a937b7c66c1f6d012bbb6f3/76cfbc9582bff9131be8e0d8d7c52274a392e044e8315e4d4f5947cf623dc4c9" :answer/id #uuid "d93c3086-1a6d-505e-9e1e-8dfdbfc9c398" :answer/type :answer