671d331d97c53f2375612cbe37f808e089924829a937b7c66c1f6d012bbb6f3/6f3f5e3f5068ba8771a159b4c6fdb65177ccd1665f279491c220b948e81268a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-39240"] :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1$ corresponding to the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ respectively, where\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2} \\\\ -2{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}=3 \\\\ -2{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n6{c}_{2}=3\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=3\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-39240/selection/ma-v1/2671d331d97c53f2375612cbe37f808e089924829a937b7c66c1f6d012bbb6f3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-327160/selection/64f4c63d426cf4c461ffff6251c36f742883e2a3ee51c2587747477dcfc1ce13" :answer/id #uuid "3031a969-cd10-5dd7-ae2d-5bc9724f03e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327160/selection/de539aa8e9cc3d7cdbd8f73ddac6a7f7628b2c0497a1940720c4d9863c5395bd" :answer/id #uuid "d067f806-41db-5fd5-a465-a827fb3529b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=2[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}-4[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327160/selection/40ae436fcaccf6ca540db328a269b1326f0718410dcc7022a9ac106896b8f3f4" :answer/id #uuid "14c9dc34-d3b5-5eb9-9274-7a2b0cc32183" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=-2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+4[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327160/selection/75eb5317c803aa3ad0865da4e58ad852c37290d6d2885b87334badb4e88b8bca" :answer/id #uuid "e5eb53ea-a141-512b-82a5-48a5ba5ae65f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327160/selection/a3e489a03ab82b31f94574929590291ff14959b5ec90ab078e5dfdf82a913ee1" :answer/id #uuid "237533a6-1f35-5329-8d03-7987d58bd91d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327160/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d737e1ed-2300-51b3-8f57-3f55764d1637" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-327160/selection/a3e489a03ab82b31f94574929590291ff14959b5ec90ab078e5dfdf82a913ee1" :answer-field/choices ["q-327160/selection/64f4c63d426cf4c461ffff6251c36f742883e2a3ee51c2587747477dcfc1ce13" "q-327160/selection/de539aa8e9cc3d7cdbd8f73ddac6a7f7628b2c0497a1940720c4d9863c5395bd" "q-327160/selection/40ae436fcaccf6ca540db328a269b1326f0718410dcc7022a9ac106896b8f3f4" "q-327160/selection/75eb5317c803aa3ad0865da4e58ad852c37290d6d2885b87334badb4e88b8bca" "q-327160/selection/a3e489a03ab82b31f94574929590291ff14959b5ec90ab078e5dfdf82a913ee1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327160" :question/id #uuid "80eb2676-605e-582a-9599-b9d33bd803ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-327160" :question/problem "Find the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-4{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for the given system:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=1\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1/4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 4\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2(0)} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ 4{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 4{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=2 \\\\ 4{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{c}_{1}=-3\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${c}_{1}=-1$ into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1+{c}_{2}=2\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-327160/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "833d0ec0-d895-5d66-b2ad-d058858caf9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327160"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-326437/selection/a7f1197ae9588386d10e7870b3e9b46d3579f051a304f07d58660f7fdc15184f" :answer/id #uuid "c8dda6e0-8852-5a4d-8ad8-b443596c0fab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=-\\frac{7}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326437/selection/e40231b416b8f95404c13c943ec2903bedfe4369bf4b08dc55acc981384eecac" :answer/id #uuid "e19aaf73-8265-5e1d-8141-af0389a0b29e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}-\\frac{7}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326437/selection/fbe75269849d684e2ef36b223b4970403a48a48786169ec52603f4e532101355" :answer/id #uuid "8c5e7375-75ea-5281-8ec4-1cc62fa4a9df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{7}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326437/selection/df5e350f0fd17f1a03c45539be12991bcc9e5631ff71119557c044c6cf96805c" :answer/id #uuid "0fe978c2-a2b9-5aad-9a8e-6d1bb46adab4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{3}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}-\\frac{9}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326437/selection/65fc853a6d6144a200386c5fa43d91391e9d8dd45b4c44e97c6aaf8dd573ac9d" :answer/id #uuid "3b00df50-0780-5999-b69f-75ac47dee284" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=-\\frac{3}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+\\frac{9}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326437/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a128bf5-933f-5d9d-a540-9c376c84eb10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-326437/selection/e40231b416b8f95404c13c943ec2903bedfe4369bf4b08dc55acc981384eecac" :answer-field/choices ["q-326437/selection/a7f1197ae9588386d10e7870b3e9b46d3579f051a304f07d58660f7fdc15184f" "q-326437/selection/e40231b416b8f95404c13c943ec2903bedfe4369bf4b08dc55acc981384eecac" "q-326437/selection/fbe75269849d684e2ef36b223b4970403a48a48786169ec52603f4e532101355" "q-326437/selection/df5e350f0fd17f1a03c45539be12991bcc9e5631ff71119557c044c6cf96805c" "q-326437/selection/65fc853a6d6144a200386c5fa43d91391e9d8dd45b4c44e97c6aaf8dd573ac9d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326437" :question/id #uuid "45696d2e-86e2-52d9-b755-e4c9e51775a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-326437" :question/problem "Find the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for the given system:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=1\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=3.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=3,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{1}+{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{c}_{1}=1 \\\\ {c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Substituting into the second equation, we obtain ${c}_{2}=-\\frac{7}{2}.$ \n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}-\\frac{7}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-326437/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "833d0ec0-d895-5d66-b2ad-d058858caf9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-326437"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327132/selection/4ad299eb55cb6cc48cd8aec1a8736b076042872747a66de2af8aedb92cc9e0d8" :answer/id #uuid "79f0f083-ecd5-53b8-acdf-1aef955c0809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=8[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327132/selection/0be9e5595e6c55726050160f03a82f0ad5d7e2cb353f4dd84ed79c0f1af680fe" :answer/id #uuid "36fc2244-c4a9-5ce0-8c3a-900a1f91647c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=-4[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327132/selection/4e8db57e6eb28da19d1936a1fd926d7821321cf5ff243ada969c45da30487c7a" :answer/id #uuid "a1375143-3704-5f19-9ef7-eb867f0f8fe1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=-3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}-8[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327132/selection/58712ccd26cd496d4ab7500b2ab709ca5e730e004aaccb88b549787a74044328" :answer/id #uuid "f456ed89-d102-5e65-8852-af4346b0d4cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=-3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+8[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327132/selection/7bc4b1a152adb7f329dce33318b727dab1ad589bf94c20573888beb08cf0894e" :answer/id #uuid "ec57dc24-c88a-555f-9cce-a026e4f0db2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=-8[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327132/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "af2b7029-f8f3-5991-9596-b360edd42294" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-327132/selection/7bc4b1a152adb7f329dce33318b727dab1ad589bf94c20573888beb08cf0894e" :answer-field/choices ["q-327132/selection/4ad299eb55cb6cc48cd8aec1a8736b076042872747a66de2af8aedb92cc9e0d8" "q-327132/selection/0be9e5595e6c55726050160f03a82f0ad5d7e2cb353f4dd84ed79c0f1af680fe" "q-327132/selection/4e8db57e6eb28da19d1936a1fd926d7821321cf5ff243ada969c45da30487c7a" "q-327132/selection/58712ccd26cd496d4ab7500b2ab709ca5e730e004aaccb88b549787a74044328" "q-327132/selection/7bc4b1a152adb7f329dce33318b727dab1ad589bf94c20573888beb08cf0894e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327132" :question/id #uuid "cdbca987-f320-5de4-ab14-d89b85df973b" :question/math-academy-id "q-327132" :question/problem "Find the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for the given system:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for the given system:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- Since $A$ is upper-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=5\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=5,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0} & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=-5 \\\\ {c}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${c}_{2}=3.$ Substituting into the first equation, we obtain ${c}_{1}=-8.$ \n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =-8[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-327132/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "833d0ec0-d895-5d66-b2ad-d058858caf9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327132"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327147/selection/dc4857de8c3c0b708d764d11125a5b9f2492e9380bc6d84fe1a5f9f5692eb345" :answer/id #uuid "39352f4d-7b43-5377-a49a-ceffcd1de0a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=2e[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{e}^{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327147/selection/ef67af62c141f4d64558f2da19aaedc910abc47a180dd12f2db65b97402c3bfc" :answer/id #uuid "8234ac2f-ef24-51a2-9745-6106106f8df3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=2[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}-3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327147/selection/b210c80057b0fa36dc4aba43d16271e45eaf16409e3dcc0d6081d38ccba2ea82" :answer/id #uuid "e17793a9-ee12-5f6c-a0b0-648fc712dc8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=e[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}-{e}^{4}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327147/selection/585c9e35b4fa3a100f4ffd8a161599d8464678418e57af736283616ff266b253" :answer/id #uuid "4fc0cd15-26c6-542f-96de-0f23572c4137" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=-2{e}^{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}-3e[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327147/selection/9647ca109c042b491a14a5eb6c5d79e00effbcad88561dcec9a2a8f8ef66cef3" :answer/id #uuid "2f27af7a-99e8-549a-86bd-c8add2d2cd12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=2e[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}-3{e}^{4}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327147/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb00aeb7-7462-55e2-9762-96fcdb85eaa1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-327147/selection/b210c80057b0fa36dc4aba43d16271e45eaf16409e3dcc0d6081d38ccba2ea82" :answer-field/choices ["q-327147/selection/dc4857de8c3c0b708d764d11125a5b9f2492e9380bc6d84fe1a5f9f5692eb345" "q-327147/selection/ef67af62c141f4d64558f2da19aaedc910abc47a180dd12f2db65b97402c3bfc" "q-327147/selection/b210c80057b0fa36dc4aba43d16271e45eaf16409e3dcc0d6081d38ccba2ea82" "q-327147/selection/585c9e35b4fa3a100f4ffd8a161599d8464678418e57af736283616ff266b253" "q-327147/selection/9647ca109c042b491a14a5eb6c5d79e00effbcad88561dcec9a2a8f8ef66cef3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327147" :question/id #uuid "96d25510-4b02-51b1-a16b-31f7b1aede10" :question/math-academy-id "q-327147" :question/problem "Find the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned},\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{4} \\\\ {e}^{4}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=0.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for the given system:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=0.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=3,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1/2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=0,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=1$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4} \\\\ {e}^{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{4} \\\\ {e}^{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{3}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 2{e}^{3}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{4} \\\\ {e}^{4}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{3}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=-2{e}^{4} \\\\ 2{e}^{3}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}={e}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second one, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{3}{c}_{1}=3{e}^{4}\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${c}_{1}=e$ into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3}(e)+{c}_{2}={e}^{4}\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=-{e}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =e[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}-{e}^{4}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-327147/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "833d0ec0-d895-5d66-b2ad-d058858caf9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327147"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186134111 :question/answer-fields 17592186131110] {:db/id "q-